      "content": "To account for unpredictable lead times like those from Shenzhen without overstocking, you should calculate separate safety stock levels for both demand variability and lead time variability, then combine them using square root addition if your data allows. This statistical approach prevents simple additive overordering while explicitly pricing in the risk of supplier delays. If your historical data on those missing shipments isn't yet quantified, consider negotiating fixed frequencies with your suppliers or gradually building a small, high-cost buffer while you invest time in analyzing the specific failure patterns of your current routes.",
